  "notes": "A formal verb used in bureaucratic and organizational contexts. The pattern is always ～に{諮|はか}る, where に marks the body being consulted.\n\nDo not confuse with other はかる verbs:\n- {測|はか}る (to measure)\n- {図|はか}る (to plan; to attempt)\n- {計|はか}る (to calculate; to time)\n- {量|はか}る (to weigh)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {委員会|いいんかい}に{諮|はか}る (to consult a committee)\n- {審議会|しんぎかい}に{諮|はか}る (to refer to an advisory council)\n- {議会|ぎかい}に{諮|はか}る (to bring before the assembly)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{諮問|しもん} (formal consultation/inquiry) is the noun form of the same concept.",
